  "# Codegen co-scientist, iteration 19

Iteration 18 recorded the amu bump that did not land: native `4f6742e` /
mir `7f7c556` took **62 failures**, `back-edge?` took that to **61**, and
`(if (string-contains? \"abcdef\" \"def\") 1 0)` still returned 0. This
file is the discrimination against the published pin, the sibling-arm
reload hole, and the executed suite after the pin moved.

Do not overwrite iteration 18. It is the record that the benchmark fixtures
were not a conformance corpus.

## Discrimination

Same host (judah), `java -cp` not `-M:test -m` (amu's test-runner main-opts
would swallow the namespace). Trees `/tmp/amu-baseline-iter18` (`d4b050ae`)
and `/tmp/amu-iter17-iter18` (`f07d260e`).

| pin | namespace | result |
|---|---|---|
| `d4b050ae` | `native-executor-test` | 57 tests / 190 assertions / **0 fail** |
| `d4b050ae` | `isa-execution-test` | 15 / 643 / **0 fail** |
| `f07d260e` | `native-executor-test` | **1 fail**: `let-composes-with-recursion-within-the-fuel-budget` (Air 4310433793, judah 4377772033) |
| `f07d260e` | `isa-execution-test` | **60 fails**: `string-contains?` / `string-replace-all`, both ISAs |

The 61 failures are a regression from call-clobber. Full-suite errors about a
missing wasm tool (`Exec failed, error: 2`) are not failures.

`kernel_call_deep_branch` still oracled correctly: it uses **call results**
after the calls, not a pre-call value in the other arm.

## The hole

`pair` then `if`; then-arm returns `acc`; else-arm uses `acc` after a
recursive call. The allocator stored n/acc at definition (slots 0/1),
reloaded **n** before the branch (dominates both arms), reloaded **acc**
into `x20` **only on the then path**, and the else `add` used `x20` with
no load. `x20` was leftover callee-saved garbage, which is why the wrong
result varied per run.

Linear last-use treats a reload in one arm as keeping the value assigned.
ADR 0012's store-at-definition does not fix lazy reloads. Iteration 18's
`back-edge?` is a different hole (textual last-use across a backward jump)
and does not see this forward split.

## The change

In `allocate-without-spills`, at every `:mir/label` after the entry, if any
currently assigned value is backed, drop those backed values from
`:assigned` and rebuild the scratch/reserve lists. The next use in that
block loads. Unbacked values stay: their definition dominates the split.

Rebuilding the lists on **every** label, including leaves with nothing
backed, scrambled the unified leaf pool and broke
`single-phi-join-coalesces-to-direct-edge-moves`. The drop is skipped when
nothing assigned is backed.

Encoding test:
`v3-else-arm-reloads-a-value-the-then-arm-already-reloaded`. That is the
same class of evidence kotoba-mir already had. The measurement is the amu
execution below.

Stacked on origin/main `799443d` (iteration 18's `back-edge?` plus
`:accepted-defective`). Did not revert all-vreg for every CFG+call.

