| kotoba-native | `e8642e0c483b9f708a1680abd692ea3ff08422e5` | pins mir `ac14016d` |
| amu | `30370f077c86de9cd47da2aaa3fc14bf0ea7e6e3` | pins native `e8642e0`; lock digest refreshed in the same commit |

west-pin-put: mir `ed9dac1a`, native `a2bb6b73`, amu `ca3ea558`.

## Execution

Judah loadavg ~1.6. After the lock refresh:

```
native-executor-test + isa-execution-test
74 tests, 841 assertions, 0 failures
```

That includes `let-composes-with-recursion-within-the-fuel-budget` and the
string-search rows. The one-line reproducer from iteration 18 is therefore
no longer the gate that holds the pin. kotoba-mir ADR 0012 is still marked
`:accepted-defective` on this pin, because that status was written before
the execution; clearing it is a later Generate, not this file rewriting 18.

kotoba-native's own suite (168 tests / 2199 assertions) was green, which
iteration 18 already said is worth nothing by itself: it does not run a
compiled program.

## What this does not change

- Timed `bench` export stays refused (iteration 4 / 5).
- Leaf vs LLVM stays refused (iteration 14). Do not rematch it here.
- fused-srem / extra MOV / FMA / PGO / kototama optimizer stay refused.
- Iteration 17's sealed +7.41% on the 24-live pair is not re-timed here.
- Straight-line ADR 0006 still storing every live-across value is a later
  Generate.
- Do not treat `kernel_call*` fixtures as a conformance corpus
  (iteration 18).

## Remaining after 19

Clear `:accepted-defective` on ADR 0012 only after a follow-up that records
this execution in that ADR. `:cfg-liveness` is still false; `back-edge?`
still sends actual loops with calls to all-vreg. That conservative floor
is not this file's ranking. Do not overwrite 04-18."}]
